meta {
  name: Webull Connectivity
  type: http
  seq: 2
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/health/webull
  body: none
  auth: none
}

headers {
  Accept: application/json
}

docs {
  # Webull Connectivity

  Actively verifies connectivity and authentication against the Webull v3 API by
  calling GET /trading/accounts/list through the direct signed-HTTP client
  (WebullV3Client). The signing is HMAC-SHA1, verified against the Webull docs'
  test vector.

  ## Outcomes
  - `200 UP` — call succeeded; `accountsFound` and the raw v3 `response` are included
  - `503 DOWN` — call failed; `httpStatus` + `rawResponse` show exactly what
    Webull returned

  Response also includes `latencyMs`, `path`, and `apiVersion` (v3).

  ## Note
  Issues a REAL authenticated request. Poll it sparingly (not on every
  load-balancer tick) to respect Webull rate limits — use GET /api/health for
  frequent liveness checks instead. Requires valid credentials
  (WEBULL_APP_KEY / WEBULL_APP_SECRET, and WEBULL_ACCESS_TOKEN if 2FA is on).
}
